WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
HOST: Welcome back to the show. Before we start, tell me a bit about where you grew up.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
GUEST: Yeah, small town, nothing special really, we just got on with things I suppose.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
HOST: And you drifted into finance from there, is that right, sort of by accident?

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
GUEST: Pretty much, one thing led to another and here we are, funny how it works.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.000
GUEST: Here's the biggest mistake I see people make with their money.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.000
They try to save whatever is left at the end of the month, and there is never anything left.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
The people who actually build wealth do the exact opposite. They save first and spend what remains.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.000
I move 20 percent into a separate account the day I get paid, before I can even see it.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:29.000
That single switch turned 200 pounds a month into over 40,000 pounds in eight years.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:35.000
And that is the real reason most people stay broke. It has almost nothing to do with their income.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.000
HOST: So going back to what you said earlier about tax, what did you mean by that?

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:21.000
GUEST: Right, so it connects to the point I made before about allowances, which is a whole other thing.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.000
GUEST: Everyone thinks you need a huge income to invest. That is completely wrong.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:51.000
The most powerful force here is time, not the size of your salary. Compounding does the heavy lifting.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:57.000
Start with 50 pounds a month at 25 and you can beat someone who starts with 500 at 40.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:02.000
That gap is not talent or luck. It is simply the years you gave your money to grow.
